Jacob: Good day. I’m Detective Trace and I’m here to investigate the disappearance of Iggy Welst.   
Ms. T: He’s – missing? I thought he was just sick, I was on my way to contact the parents... Do you know anything?
Jacob: Not yet, but that’s why I’m here after all. When did you see him last?
Ms. T: A… week ago. He was being his normal self, joking with his friends… just the usual tensions between teens that age, you know… and he also has good grades, I don’t know what might have happened to him…
Jacob: That is what I intend to find out… but silence isn’t necessarily a bad thing.
Jacob: … You mentioned his friends. Have they said anything that might help me find him?
Ms. T: I can’t really think of anything at the moment… well, some others have also been sick but they’re friends, maybe there is a disease going around.
Jacob: Remember something else, something that happend a few days or weeks ago ?
Ms. T: Well, come to think of it, I think they may have been wrangling.
Jacob: They were fighting?... hm…
Jacob: Do you know where i can find them or one of thier usual hangout places?
Ms. T: Well … a lot of students go to the new ice creme shop that opened recently down the road, maybe you can find them there?
Jacob: Alright… thank you for your cooperation, I will come back to you if I have further questions.
Ms. T: No problem at all… let me know in any way if I can help… I hope they are alright… good luck.
Jacob: Thank you.
Jacob: New ice creme shop huh… might be worth checking out, maybe someone there saw something.
=> END

